Shippo Integration Deep Dive

What we're replacing / augmenting

Right now the platform uses static lookup tables (STATE_ZONE, SHIPPING_MID) duplicated in 3 places (frontend shipping.js, frontend shipping-rates.js, and backend views.py) to estimate shipping. Sellers
manually type tracking numbers. There's no label generation, no real carrier rates, and no automated delivery detection.

Shippo replaces all of that.

---

What Shippo gives us

┌─────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Feature │ What it does for PartBridge │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Real-time carrier rates │ Actual USPS/UPS/FedEx prices per item based on real dims + ZIP pair │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Label purchase │ Seller buys postage in one click, gets printable PDF │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Tracking number │ Auto-returned with label — no manual entry │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Tracking webhooks │ TRACK_UPDATED → we auto-flip order to Delivered │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Address validation │ Validate buyer address at checkout before payment │
├─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Void/refund label │ If order cancelled, void unused label to reclaim postage │
└─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

---

Architecture overview

Checkout (buyer)
├── POST /orders/shipping/rates/ ← new
│ Shippo.Shipment.create() → return rate array to frontend
└── Buyer picks a rate per item ← rate_object_id stored

Place Order
└── CartCheckoutView stores shippo_shipment_id + rate_object_id
on ShippingRequest (not yet charged, label not yet bought)

Seller action (after payment captured)
└── POST /orders/sales/{id}/buy-label/ ← new
Shippo.Transaction.create(rate_object_id)
→ stores tracking_number, label_url, actual_cost
→ Order.status → SHIPPED

Shippo Webhook
└── POST /api/shippo/webhook/ ← new
TRACK_UPDATED + status=DELIVERED → \_mark_order_delivered()

