Checkout flow summary by size

Small / Medium

1. Buyer enters ZIP
2. Frontend: POST /orders/shipping/rates/ per item
3. Buyer sees real carrier options, picks one
4. Checkout POST carries { shipping_selections: { item_id: { rate_object_id, amount } } }
5. Backend creates ShippingRequest: shipping_type=shippo, shippo_rate_object_id=..., quoted_cost=actual rate
6. Stripe PI created for real total

Large (Freight)

1. Frontend shows freight ($450–$650 est.) vs economy ($100) selector
2. Buyer picks Freight
3. Checkout POST: shipping_mode=freight
4. Backend creates ShippingRequest: shipping_type=freight, freight_quote_amount=midpoint
5. Stripe PI includes freight estimate in total
   --- post payment ---
6. Admin arranges carrier, adds TrackingUpdate records manually
7. Admin calls freight-settle with actual_cost
8. If actual < quoted → Stripe partial refund issued automatically
9. If actual > quoted → buyer notified, can accept or cancel
10. If cancel then everything goes back to its place, item becomes active again, order cancels, user receives money
    Large (Economy) / XL

11. Checkout POST: shipping_mode=economy
12. Backend creates ShippingRequest: shipping_type=economy, quoted_cost=$100/$150
13. Admin fulfills manually
14. Admin adds TrackingUpdate records
15. Admin marks delivered → order closes

---

Public tracking URL flow

1. When ShippingRequest is created (at checkout), tracking_token is auto-generated (e.g. secrets.token_urlsafe(16))
2. Buyer order detail page shows: "Track your package → partbridge.com/tracking/abc123"
3. Page is public — no login needed (so buyers can share links)
4. For Shippo items: real carrier updates shown (populated via webhook)
5. For freight/economy: admin-entered updates shown with timestamps

